// Deliberate collision fixture for cratestack#802: model `Post` derives the
// hook `useCreatePostMutation` under `--tanstack`
// (`templates/src/rest-react-query.ts.j2:62`), and `mutation procedure
// create_post` derives the same identifier through `to_pascal_case` — the
// snake_case spelling on purpose, since the collision is NOT limited to
// procedure names that are already PascalCase; both run through the same
// `split_words` tokenizer.
//
// Unlike #777's `--swr` case this is a SAME-FILE collision: both hook
// families are emitted into `src/react-query.ts`, so `tsc` reports TS2393
// (duplicate function implementation) and TS2323 (cannot redeclare
// exported variable) rather than TS2308 on a barrel. Those codes were
// measured by generating this fixture with the check disabled and running
// real `tsc` — not taken from #802, which predicted TS2300.
//
// `create`, not `list` (inherited reasoning from
// `swr_procedure_name_collision.cstack`, cratestack#784): `create` is the
// one operation whose derived name and whose generated Rust axum handler
// disagree on plurality — `createPost`/`CreatePost` against
// `handle_create_posts` — so it is the only one of the five that reaches
// this generator at all. `procedure list_posts` is also `model Post`'s
// `handle_list_posts`, which `cratestack-parser`'s
// `validate::procedure_handler_collisions` rejects first, so a fixture
// built on it could never exercise this check.
//
// `mutation`, explicitly: the hook suffix follows the procedure kind, and
// only a mutation produces the `useCreatePostMutation` spelling that
// collides here. The query-suffix half is covered by
// `tanstack_query_hook_collision.cstack`.
//
// `@@allow("create", ...)` is load-bearing: without a `create` rule the
// model has no create hook, `emitted_model_hook_names` omits
// `useCreatePostMutation` entirely, and there would be nothing to collide
// with.

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

auth SessionUser {
  id Int
}

model Post {
  id Int @id
  title String

  @@allow("read", true)
  @@allow("create", auth() != null)
}

mutation procedure create_post(): Post
  @allow(auth() != null)
